---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_298",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 298,
  "text": "[[1331.9]] <b>244.  Ordinis, loci, temporis particulae«. Aus und zu Caspar Schoppe, Paradoxa literaria [Ende 1685 bis Anfang 1686 (?)]</b>\n[[1331.10]] SCHOPPE, PARADOXA LITERARIA\n [[1331.11]] <tab/>[Ende 1685 bis Anfang 1686 (?)]\n[[1331.15]] <b>Ordinis, loci, temporis particulae</b> </p>\n<p> [[1331.16]] [p. 1 sq.] <i>Principium</i> idem quod <i>principio</i>. <i>Principium hoc oro</i> Afranius apud Charisium\n[[1331.17]] vid. Sciopp. ad Hier. Aleandrum (<i>Paradox. lit. I</i>.); de illo Johannis VIII. <i>princi-\n[[1331.18]] pium qui et loquor vobis</i>. De quo loco ait se dissentire ab Aleandro, qui nescio quo in\n[[1331.19]] libello explicuerat. <i>Nisi enim me fallit</i> (inquit Scioppius) <i>in Graeco est</i> <greek>th̀n ărxh́n</greek>. <i>Ut</i>\n[[1332.1]] <i>sensus sit, Ego idem ipse sum, qui et principium«</i> (id est <i>principio</i>, ut <i>primum</i> pro <i>primo</i>)\n[[1332.2]] <i>vobis locutus sum</i>«. Nimirum ut a Graecis particula <greek>katà</greek> per Ellipsin supprimitur.\n[[1332.3]] Cicero et Varro interrogati, utrum dici deberet <i>tertium Consul</i>, an <i>tertio Consul</i>, ille\n[[1332.4]] haesit, et <i>Tert.</i> scribendum dixit, hic inaniter distinxit apud A. Gell. lib. 10 c. 1, cum\n[[1332.5]] tamen nihil intersit ut exemplis docet Scioppius. </p>\n<p> [[1332.6]] [p. 3 sq.] <i>Primo</i> intelligi potest <i>loco</i>, quod tamen pro <i>tempore</i> sumitur. Ita <i>hoc loco</i>\n[[1332.7]] pro <i>tum</i> Cicero dixit 15 <i>ad Att.</i> 11. Et Terentius <i>loco motum</i> dixit, qui suam horam non\n[[1332.8]] obtinet, in Prologo <i>Phorm.</i> Ubi Donatum videre est operae pretium. Hyginus <i>fabula</i> 273.\n[[1332.9]] <i>Nono loco facti sunt ludi in Nemea Archemoro.</i> <i>Nono loco</i>, id est <i>nona vice</i>, seu <i>nono.</i> </p>\n<p> [[1332.10]] <i>E loco</i>, vel <i>in loco</i> (+ e vestigio <i>sur le champ</i> +), id est <i>statim</i>, unde factum est, <i>illico</i>\n[[1332.11]] vel <i>inlico</i>, pro quo Hispani hodieque <i>luego.</i> Et Plautus in <i>Aul.</i> act. 4 sc. 8. <i>Effodio aulam\n[[1332.12]] auri plenam, inde exeo. Loco</i> (statim) <i>video recipere se senem, ille me non videt.</i> Hic <i>loco</i>\n[[1332.13]] eodem prorsus modo dixit quo saepe alias <i>numero</i>. Etiam <i>pedatum</i> aut <i>pedatu</i> in similibus\n[[1332.14]] exaudiri potest, quod significat congressum, Italice <i>voltam</i>, Hispanice <i>vicem</i> (quod\n[[1332.15]] Horatiano illo tuebimur <i>plus vice simplici</i>), Germanice <i>mahl</i>, id est convivium, quia\n[[1332.16]] publicos congressus conviviis notabant, ex quo saepe <i>Malli</i> in latinis Germanicorum\n[[1332.17]] populorum legibus pro conventibus publicis leguntur. </p>\n<p> [[1332.18]] [p. 4 sq.] Plaut. <i>Cist. nisi pedatu tertio omnes afflixero</i> (+ <i>au troisième pas</i> +). Cato:\n[[1332.19]] <i>Igitur tertio pedatu bellum nobis fecere.</i> Idem: <i>his duobus bellis alteras</i> (id est Festo\n[[1332.20]] autore <i>alias</i> seu <i>ad alias res</i>, <i>caetera</i>, <greek>tà ^%)/alla</greek>) <i>stipendio agrique parte multati, alteras\n[[1332.21]] oppidum vi captum.</i> Haec verba declarans Charisius ait <i>alteras</i> idem valere, quod <i>primo\n[[1332.22]] et secundo pedatu</i>. Porro cum <i>alteras</i> vel <i>alias</i> dicitur <i>Res</i> subintelligi patet, nempe <i>Res\n[[1332.23]] temporis</i> vel <i>loci</i>, hoc est <i>locum</i> seu <i>tempus</i>. </p>\n<p> [[1332.24]] Quomodo Graecorum more <i>rem voluptatum</i> Plautus dixit pro <i>voluptate</i>. Et Phaedrus\n[[1332.25]] <i>rem cibi</i> pro <i>cibo</i>. Plautus <i>Epid.</i> a. 4 sc. 2 <i>meus servus eam rem sobrie et frugaliter\n[[1332.26]] accuravit, ut alias res</i> (<greek>tà ^%)/alla</greek>) <i>ille est impense improbus</i>. Ita est in omnibus libris, nisi\n[[1333.1]] quos Lambinus et Douza depravarunt. Sic pro <i>alias</i> dicitur <i>caetera, ad caetera.</i> Sic\n[[1333.2]] Virgilius, <i>prima, postrema</i>, quasi <i>ad prima, quoad prima.</i> 3tio <i>Aen.</i> <i>Prima, hominis facies\n[[1333.3]] et pulcro pectore virgo, pubetenus, postrema immani corpore pistrix</i>. Ubi Servius:\n[[1333.4]] <i>prima« est nominativus pluralis a Neutro, et est figura Graeca</i>, <greek>tà prṽta ^%)/anurvpow</greek>.\n[[1333.5]] De figura recte ille, sed quod nominativum dixit, fugit eum ratio, est enim accusativus\n[[1333.6]] dependens a praepositione <greek>katá</greek>, ut illud Christi superius <greek>th̀n ărxh́n</greek>. </p>\n<p> [[1333.7]] Caeterum pro <i>loco, pedatu</i>, et similibus dicitur etiam <i>numero</i>, item <i>pretio.</i> Ut\n[[1333.8]] dicimus <i>esse aliquo vel nullo numero, loco, pretio.</i> Sedigitus Volcatius de comicis: <i>Dein\n[[1333.9]] Naevius qui servet pretio in tertio est</i>. Plaut. <i>Poen.</i> a. 1 sc. 2 <i>primum prima salva sis et\n[[1333.10]] secunda tu secundo salve in pretio, tertia salve extra pretium</i>. <i>Menaechm.</i> act. 1 sc. 3\n[[1333.11]] <i>Anime mi Menaechme salve. PEN. Quid ego? ER. Extra numerum es mihi</i>. </p>\n",
  "number": "244.",
  "title": "Ordinis, loci, temporis particulae«. Aus und zu Caspar Schoppe, Paradoxa literaria",
  "date": "[Ende 1685 bis Anfang 1686 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:244. Ordinis, loci, temporis particulae«. Aus und zu Caspar Schoppe, Paradoxa literaria [Ende 1685 bis Anfang 1686 (?)] SCHOPPE, PARADOXA LITERARIA [Ende 1685 bis Anfang 1686 (?)] Ordinis, loci, temporis particulae [p. 1 sq.] Principium idem quod principio. Principium hoc oro Afranius apud Charisium...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>